    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense is primed for a high-ceiling performance today, spearheaded by **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who headline our daily efficiency scores at 81.88 and 73.10, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** occupies the top spot in the lineup against Severino, benefiting from a potent combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park (+16%) and a strong SP skill matchup (+15%), making him our most reliable engine for R and SB production. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** finds himself in an ideal spot against Alcantara; the dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) and the SP matchup boost (+11%) maximize his output potential, cementing his status as a must-start. **Kyle Tucker** and **Jacob Wilson** also project as elite plays, with the latter benefiting significantly from a park factor (+16%) that elevates his baseline projection well into the strong-start category.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Nasim Nunez**, who hovered at a 53.72 score\u2014respectable enough to warrant consideration\u2014but ultimately fell short due to his #9 position in the batting order. While the matchup against Alcantara offers a slight boost for his SB potential due to the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, the lack of RBI and R upside from the bottom of the order made him a clear cut behind the higher-scoring **Josh Jung** and **Brady House**. We must also monitor the status of **Sam Antonacci** and **Heliot Ramos** closely; while **Sam Antonacci** holds an elite xwOBA, he faces the stiffest test of the day against Gilbert. The SP skill deficit (-19%) is a major warning, signaling that despite his offensive tools, his efficiency could fluctuate against a pitcher of that caliber. With **Luis Robert Jr.** remaining sidelined on the IL, the Waves must lean on the depth of our outfield unit to compensate for his absence in the SB category.",
